{
  "raw": {
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912162655251599~1/edit": {
      "title": "Casual -  Integrity Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/10/2026 Department: Office of Centre for Education and Innovation Location: VIC Job No: APTEO131434#001 Expressions of interest sought for Casual - Integrity Compliance Officers. Multiple casual positions. Located at Melbourne campus. About the role: Provide effective and proactive administration support to ensure a consistent and equitable approach to administrative processes across all stages of Academic Integrity case management. Maintain accurate and timely records within Student Academic Misconduct Management System (SAMMS) Draft, review and finalise student correspondence, including emails, formal letters (using approved templates) with a focus on accuracy, clarity and tone appropriate to the nature of academic integrity matters. Ensure compliant document retention and recording keeping within Student System (Banner). Monitor and respond to internal and external queries within Academic Integrity Inbox, ensuring timely, professional and consistent communication. You will need to have: Prior experience working in a same or similar role or within the University sector. Demonstrated high level of written, oral and interpersonal communication skills. Comprehensive IT skills, including use of enterprise systems, administering databases and working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to use initiative, high degree of accuracy, to exercise good judgement, and to deliver quality outcomes, with the ability to act with discretion and sensitivity and to maintain confidentiality. Applicants should demonstrate awareness of the University's Mission and Catholic ethos and demonstrate an understanding of how this role serves the Mission. Applicants should demonstrate commitment to cultural diversity and ethical practice principles and demonstrate knowledge of equal employment opportunity and workplace health and safety, appropriate to the level of the appointment, The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. How to Apply: To lodge an expression of interest click the 'Apply' button and attach a brief cover letter indicating what availability you have inclusive of hours per week, your contact details, your CV (inclusive of the qualifications you hold). Click here for further information on casual employment at ACU. General enquiries can be sent to Montanna Motti, Academic Integrity Coordinator - Office of Centre for Education and Innovation, Montanna.Motti@acu.edu.au Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers Applications close: 15-OCT-26 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912162259066699~1/edit": {
      "title": "Digital Demand Manager (Front Door)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Department: Digital Innovation and Emerging Technology Location: NSW,QLD,VIC Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Brisbane, Australia | Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV128265#021 New opportunity to lead intake, prioritisation and shaping of digital initiatives partnering with stakeholders to align business needs with delivery outcomes Join a newly formed specialist AI team committed to improving operational efficiencies and delivering innovation at ACU ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney, Melbourne or Brisbane campus About the role: Operating within Digital Innovation & Emerging Technology , the Digital Demand Manager (Front Door) is accountable for the design, implementation and continuous evolution of ACU's enterprise demand and capacity management strategy, framework and governance model. This position manages the flow of work across the Information Technology Directorate (ITD) and provides a central point of coordination for demand ensuring requests are effectively assessed, prioritised and routed to optimise delivery outcomes and utilisation of team capacity including engagement with strategic delivery partners. The Digital Demand Manager has high visibility of demand, capacity and delivery performance through reporting and stakeholder communication enabling informed decision making across IT and the university. Working closely with delivery teams, ITD Senior Leadership and the Finance & Planning Business Partner the role aligns demand with available capacity, funding and resource allocation. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Brett Wiskar, National Manager, Digital Innovation & Change at: Brett.Wiskar@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $160,162 - $170,900 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $135,360 - $144,538 (pro rata) pa (HEW 9), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 18-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912168272709999~1/edit": {
      "title": "Team Leader",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Department: National School of Allied Health Location: NSW,QLD Campus Location: North Sydney, Australia | Brisbane, Australia Job No: APTAV102103#099 Exceptional opportunity to lead admin and operational functions to support the School of Allied Health Manage a dedicated team delivering high quality administration, coordination and support services ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Full time, permanent opportunity with some hybrid flexibility working at North Sydney or Brisbane campus About the role: Operating within National School of Allied Health , the Team Leader will be responsible for delivering administrative leadership and organisational functionality to support the administrative operations and day to day business of the School of Allied Health. The position leads the Administrative Officers, Project Officers and functions and ensures provision of high quality administrative and coordination support, timely and accurate information and advice, and delivery of reception and support services. The Team Leader will manage processes involved in course administration, staffing administration, promotion and profiling of the school, resource administration and various other operations of the school. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to James Morrison, Team Leader - National School of Allied Health at: james.morrison@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $124,509 - $134,699 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $105,212 - $113,823 (pro rata) pa (HEW 7), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 18-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. #LI-DNI ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
    },
    "https://candidate.aurion.cloud/acu/production/career/vacancies/2912176248040699~1/edit": {
      "title": "Technical Services Officer, Simulation",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Department: Technical Services Location: VIC Campus Location: Melbourne, Australia Job No: APTAV103704#030 Support daily operations and deliver high quality technical and laboratory services for Faculty of Health Sciences Work with a motivated team providing safe, compliant and functional learning and teaching environments ACU offers 17% employer superannuation, salary packaging and generous leave provisions Part time 4 days (28 hours)/week, continuing opportunity working at Melbourne campus About the role: Operating within Technical Services , the Technical Services Officer, Simulation supports the daily operations of ACU's Technical Services, provides high quality laboratory and technical services, and ensures university expectations are consistently met for the Faculty of Health Sciences learning environments. Working closely with the Technical Service team and academics, the position will be responsible for preparing, set up and resetting of learning and teaching activities, maintaining equipment and facilities, and managing compliance and risk management in line with work health and safety requirements to ensure environments are safe, functional and fit for purpose. The Technical Services Officer may also have responsibility for coordinating the Technical Assistants. For full position details, refer to the position description Contact: General enquiries can be sent to Jeremy Fowler, National Manager - Technical Services at: jeremy.fowler@acu.edu.au What we offer: The University pursues an excellence agenda and offers an environment where staff are welcomed and safe, and valued through development, participation and involvement. Total remuneration valued to $101,464 - $109,838 total rem (pro rata) pa, including salary component $85,739 - $92,815 (pro rata) pa (HEW 5), employer contribution to superannuation and annual leave loading. 17% employer superannuation contributions to eligible continuing and fixed-term staff. Annual leave loading of an equivalent to 17.5% of four weeks' salary pro rata payable, dependent on your commencement date. As an ACU staff member, you will have access to generous benefits which include but not limited to: flexible work, study leave, a variety of leave provisions and salary packaging. Find out more information about the benefits or working at ACU here . How to Apply: Step 1: Review the Position Description and become familiar with Our Mission and the Application process Step 2: Click the 'View Position Description and Apply' button, and populate your candidate application details, including your: Resume. Recommended responses to the Selection Criteria and Core Competencies in a cover letter (maximum 2 pages) or in the online Declaration and Criteria application page. Brief online responses to any pre-screening employment questions. Applications close: 18-OCT-2026 at 11:59pm AUS Eastern Standard Time Preferred candidates will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks, including those related to gender-based violence and foreign interference, in line with ACU's compliance requirements. Candidates must hold Australian work rights to apply for this position. For permanent/ continuing roles, applicants must have permanent work rights. For further information visit Immigration and Citizenship(homeaffairs.gov.au) Your Privacy of personal information is maintained in accordance with ACU policy. For more details visit: www.acu.edu.au/careers ACU is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace culture that values diversity and enables our people to reach their potential. This is underpinned by our mission and values, grounded in our respect for all people and the advancement of the common good. In line with our commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion we welcome candidates from all backgrounds and lived experiences. ACU is recognised as a Veteran Employment Supporter and veterans are encouraged to apply. ACU offers support for candidates that may require adjustments through the recruitment process. Please contact recruitment@acu.edu.au to discuss your requirements in confidence. About ACU: Australian Catholic University (ACU) is a publicly funded university whose teaching, research and service is shaped by the vision of flourishing lives, thriving communities, and a more ethical future for our world. ACU has more than 2,500 staff and 34,000 students across eight campuses: Ballarat, Brisbane, Canberra, Melbourne, North Sydney, Strathfield, Blacktown and Rome. ACU draws on the Catholic intellectual tradition which values human reason and welcomes everyone regardless of their faith, cultural tradition or circumstances. ACU invites all staff - both academic and professional - to embrace, and to support in ways meaningful to them, its mission to respect the dignity of every human person, to seek knowledge and to advance the common good. ACU does not accept candidate applications submitted by external recruitment agencies through the ACU careers website. Learn more about Athena Swan"
